A||N||8||Greg Piet||First Rallycross||||7||
Z||000000||Greg Piet||03-20-2000||02:40 PM||||Well I did it!  I took the Fiero out in the dirt!  I did really well which surprised me, with it being my first rallyX.  I feel I must share this moral victory with all you other Fiero Nuts!<BR>There was a guy with a mitsubishi eclipse which had abot 20 sponsorship stickers, and other performance parts stickers.  Each sticker corresponded to a part installed in the car.  He had the full racing suit, roll cage, and about 15K of performance parts upgrades in the eclipse.  Well I beat him with my MSD ignition, rear sway bar, and short shifter stock Fiero by a couple of seconds for the total time.  It felt good!<P>There were some hardcore ProRally drivers out there, and when it was all done a few of them came over to me and said "Hey Rookie!  You did really good!"<P>So I guess the stock Fiero can still kick ass!<P>P.S.  Driving home the car was shaking like a beast.  I figure it is the alignment.  letting go of the wheel, the car still tracked well, but it seemed like the back end was shaking.  Im thinking i screwed up my alignment, but it might just be dirt stuck in the wheels causing them to be unbalanced.  It only shook above 55mph, and got really bad above 65.  Any guesses?  Will I have problems getting the alignment fixed at a Sears or somewhere(I've only taken cars to Sears to do alignments)?  ||||reg||7
Z||000001||DRH||03-20-2000||03:03 PM||||Congrats on the race!<P>You might have knocked off a wheel weight???<BR>||||reg||3
Z||000002||Spyder||03-21-2000||12:48 PM||||Greg,<BR>Sounds like you had fun, and got some respect.<BR>Congratulations!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Greg Piet||03-30-2000||04:42 AM||||Well Finally they posted the Pics from the rallycross I attended.<P>I made the cut apparently, and a Pic of my Fiero and I are on the website!<P>Here is the link <A HREF="http://www.lvrscca.org/photos/rx20000319/page2.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.lvrscca.org/photos/rx20000319/page2.html</A> ||||reg||1
